      "id": "claim_59f0573c28d046119a9eb91f24fcb331",
      "statement": "A 401 on a still-current token is handled as an application-state transition, not a form error: the HTTP client clears the token and calls notifySessionExpired(); AuthProvider subscribes via onSessionExpired — the framework-agnostic listener registry in lib/api/session.ts — sets sessionExpired and logs out, while a late 401 from an older request (token already rotated) and unauthenticated 401s such as bad login credentials remain ordinary request errors.",
